A||||2||mshill||Questions for 3.4 pushrod gurus...||||5||
Z||000000||mshill||11-14-2000||01:53 AM||||I am prepping my 95 3.4L Camaro block for the installation.  I am hoping to have it done around Thanksgiving timeframe.  I have some questions for the experts out there:<P>1) What is the 1/2 hole in the top of the block (accompanied by a small tapped hole on one side) in front of the intake manifold and just behind the timing cover?  What do you block it with?<P>2) I am replacing an 86GT 2.8 with it.  Should I use my 2.8 timing cover and oil pan or just leave the stock 3.4 stuff on it?<P>3) Anyone out there drilled their own starter holes?  Does someone have a template or jig I can borrow?<P>4) What have most done with the missing (the third) bolt hole for the AC bracket and engine shock mount?  I think Ed Parks welds a  stud to the block.  Will it hold with just two bolts?<P>Thanks guys.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||11-14-2000||03:31 AM||||ok, here are the answers (and, by the way, I am STILL trying to work out a trip up there to get those parts!!) --<P>(1) there is a plug (actually a sensor) on the the 3.4 block that just needs to have the wires cut - leave it in the hole to plug it.<P>(2) you can use the 2.8 timing cover but you need to trim out the inside of the 2.8 oil pan.<P>(3) we drill the starter holes on our 3.4 conversions and have a jig here.<P>(4) you need to weld a stud to the bracket....<P>call us here at the shop and we'll step you through all of this if you want -- 1-510-233-4376<P>------------------<BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                             <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||12-01-2000||05:07 PM||||terry,  the cam position sensor was missing from my block.  What can I use to plug the hole?  I tried both a 3/4 inch freeze plug (too small) and a 20mm freeze plug (too big).<P>Anyone out there have a cam position sensor for a 3.4L OHV engine?<P>BTW, thanks for taking all of that stuff on the side of my yard.  My son said you took everything and he was right.||||reg||13
